Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think maybe by now the book, I'm not sure if it's empty, but Wolfram is going to tell us,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.64,0:00:06.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think, his thoughts about what are the remaining challenges if we want to realize embodied AI.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.24,0:00:09.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let's give a warm welcome to Wolfram.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.48,0:00:13.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Dieter.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.64,0:00:14.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's take a selfie.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.31,0:00:19.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.75,0:00:22.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And thanks for having me here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.33,0:00:25.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,I must confess, I'm super nervous right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.83,0:00:30.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's actually my very first plenary speech in robotics,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.43,0:00:37.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,at least in the robotics and automation society space, and never stood in front of such a big audience.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.75,0:00:40.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so it's really great to be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.81,0:00:47.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,This talk is a little bit about my perspective or my vision on where
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.49,0:00:54.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,we might be going in this right now race about embodied AI systems or robots.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.91,0:01:01.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it also will, I will take you back a little bit, maybe like 30 years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.53,0:01:07.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,But at some point in time, we'll even take you even further back, something like two to 3000 years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.49,0:01:09.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,I will let you know at that particular time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.49,0:01:14.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we will then see what is behind all of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.48,0:01:20.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this talk would not be possible with all my friends and colleagues, normally talks end with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.12,0:01:22.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm going to start with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.70,0:01:28.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have so many friends who contributed to that that I cannot actually add pictures, would have taken me years.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.18,0:01:37.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,I thank all my friends and colleagues who contributed to that work, and a few will be listed and even be shown in pictures here in this presentation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.33,0:01:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So my view in robotics is actually that that we are going to be or to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.16,0:01:51.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,have a that we are having actually super useful tool for helping us solving important societal problems.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.54,0:01:57.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let it be traffic and it can be particularly seen here where you can actually see
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.38,0:02:05.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,multiple companies with driverless cars driving around making our traffic more effective and also hopefully safer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.62,0:02:11.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can be the case in production where we are in a global race about the most efficient
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.30,0:02:20.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,production systems and so on and where we are believing that robotics will help us competing in that space.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.01,0:02:25.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then there is assistance and healthcare, the next dimension, we will talk about this as well,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.81,0:02:32.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,this question of how can we actually build robots that help us with elderly care and also support us in our homes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.39,0:02:39.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And finally we are living on a finite sphere and actually constantly growing the fastest growth is
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.81,0:02:46.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,in this space here this room it's probably this fastest growing society on earth and that's also something
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.63,0:02:53.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we need to support or hoped to be able to support with robotics and in fact for
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.20,0:02:59.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we need that what is called intelligent robots robots that perceive their world like maybe reason about
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.12,0:03:04.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,it create models about it and then execute actions in order to achieve their goals That's basically
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.76,0:03:10.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,that what we are interested in and right now we are working on that what is called embodied
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.08,0:03:17.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,robotics and or embodied AI as a potential solution to this and I love these Pictures with humanoids
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.90,0:03:25.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,all these, by the way, disclaimer: all pictures that contain white humanoids are generated with generative AI, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.52,0:03:29.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,all the others are basically handmade and And here are a couple of solutions where we
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.82,0:03:35.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,envision this to be done in mostly like right now using that what is called humanoid robots.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.70,0:03:40.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,The reason why humanoids are envisioned to be one of the solutions here is that
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.34,0:03:47.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,they will allow us to make a smooth transition from actually manual production towards automated production.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.98,0:03:50.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we can even have this what is called mixed production,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.82,0:03:59.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,where we have human and robot co-workers in the same space on the same tasks with the same tools, basically accomplishing the very same tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.18,0:04:02.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is why humanoids are so much hyped these days.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.46,0:04:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,But on top of this, there's also the next hype.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.72,0:04:13.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was in China twice this year and saw like several hundred startups in the space of humanoid robots.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.54,0:04:17.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And on top of this, equally many startups in the space of robotic hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.06,0:04:24.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for this is that in order to perform dexterous manipulations with tools that we also use we need to have proper hands But it's not
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.32,0:04:29.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,only about mechanics It's also about perception and now we'll come to this in
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.28,0:04:33.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,this talk as well And finally and this was mentioned by Peter stone earlier today.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.00,0:04:45.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,You also need Computing on a large scale and on a larger scale than it was available thus far for at least university-like research.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.06,0:04:53.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,But on top of this, and this is something that is mostly underestimated by investors and so on and so forth and even politicians,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.94,0:05:02.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,is this problem of building an AI system that can actually control these robots to accomplish these tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.72,0:05:08.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have made an enormous progress over the past years when it comes to building the hardware for this,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.58,0:05:17.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,also enhance humanoids for me it's has been just crazy but building the AI is still the challenge that we are
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.14,0:05:24.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,facing right and now ask like robot learning is it right and that's actually what I believe right the only way
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.72,0:05:33.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,for solving this is right robot learning and if you boil this even further down then this is this community over
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.56,0:05:40.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,here it's basically the core community that is working on this topic and where I believe this is going to take us,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.66,0:05:43.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,hopefully, there where we want to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.39,0:05:49.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is our journey more than 2,000 years back.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.37,0:05:55.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is, according to Greek mythology, this is the King Sisyphus.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.41,0:06:07.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And he was, because he believed that he was more intelligent than Zeus, the most important god in Greek mythology, and Zeus didn't really like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.39,0:06:13.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Turns out that kind of like reflects also sometimes our thinking here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.50,0:06:17.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everyone of us believes to be the most intelligent person in the world, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.48,0:06:19.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's something that researchers mostly need to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.24,0:06:26.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Zeus got so upset about this that he condemned Sisyphus to actually take a large boulder up a hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.98,0:06:32.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this thing here is the boulder that this poor guy was condemned to transport up the hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.40,0:06:35.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not that this was enough of a for this guy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.66,0:06:43.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Zeus actually condemned this Boulder so that it always fell down when Sisyphus was close to the summit of this mountain And
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.94,0:06:50.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,then the boulder actually rolled down the entire hill and this guy had to start from scratch You might not ask this question.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.64,0:06:52.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,What does this have to do with our research?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.90,0:07:00.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's basically that like when you look at that what we are doing is we are basically Finding some sort of technology.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.57,0:07:02.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let it be Probabilistic Robotics.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.63,0:07:05.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let it be deep learning Let it be foundation models, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.01,0:07:10.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are believing that this technology is finally going to help us getting this boulder
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.97,0:07:16.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,up the hill and Unfortunately so far right you were not really successful with this,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.65,0:07:17.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.15,0:07:25.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So somehow like some God actually through this boulder again down and this road down and yet to start from scratch again This is why what
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.31,0:07:33.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,this has from my perspective to do or this see like kind of the metaphor that is matching that what has actually happened in in our
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.31,0:07:37.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,community and when you look at technologies I've been involved in the detail
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.89,0:07:41.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,already mentioned I mean there have been three important boulders that I worked
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.79,0:07:47.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,on and it started in 1995 who actually was born at that time
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.33,0:07:55.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,already 1995 five percent or so of this audience here right which is which
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.76,0:08:00.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,is pretty cool this when we actually started working on this with the
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.12,0:08:06.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,belief that we could actually solve everything by probabilistic reasoning right and like
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.20,0:08:17.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,this was basically the time when we created this book, Probabilistic Robotics; there is Sebastian, Dieter and me right in
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.48,0:08:28.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,car at that point in time which basically came out of this of the success of the Probabilistic Robotics theory or like concept in the context
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.12,0:08:34.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,of Autonomous driving right and to here in the bottom you even see the three of us on the summit of the mount of a mountain Unfortunately,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.54,0:08:38.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's not the same mountains to the first force condemned to carry the boulder up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.74,0:08:48.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was from Mount Rainier instead so so this is basically the equations that are underlying there and that led to an enormous success in the space
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.24,0:08:53.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,of Autonomous driving and it's basically that what you see outside these self
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.06,0:08:59.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,-driving cars are basically governed by this equation over here which is state estimation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.24,0:09:04.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we are basically trying to figure out where the vehicle is given a map of the environment.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.56,0:09:10.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when it comes to building self-driving cars, you need to solve basically three tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.78,0:09:13.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first one is stay on the road, which is localization.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.66,0:09:15.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,The second one is don't get hit.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.54,0:09:17.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the third one is don't hit anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.30,0:09:21.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And once you are able to do all this, you're getting really, really far.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.90,0:09:29.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here's this entire thing in action in indoors and outdoors and GPS denied environments and then you ask
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.06,0:09:34.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,the question like how accurate is this actually we also did some experiments a few years ago just to give
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.28,0:09:42.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,you an intuition how accurately you can actually localize a robot on a factory floor then these black stripes here
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.04,0:09:48.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,that are not used for localization they are actually indicating how accurate this platform is when you want to see
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.70,0:09:55.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,this in more quantities then you can see down here in these statistics that the accuracy in localization in post
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.62,0:10:05.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,estimation is around a millimeter and who believes that this can be achieved with foundation models as well nobody okay
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.01,0:10:13.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,I maybe in a few years from now detail as well which is good so but this is kind of
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.11,0:10:23.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,like the the outcome of this endeavor Probabilistic Robotics and that led to these self driving cars and you can
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.45,0:10:31.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,see a typical software stack of self-driving cars and those components where I think Probabilistic Robotics is particularly
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.27,0:10:40.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,strong and it's in fact this mapping and localization task here is an application to to mapping it's basically the
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.07,0:10:47.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,equations underlying slam and this is a company that I found a ten years ago that is like concerned with
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.59,0:10:54.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,3d mapping of real estate buildings and also historic buildings also several hundred years ago like the Leaning Tower of
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.89,0:11:01.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Pisa we created with this technology the most accurate model of this of this tower it's an indoor outdoor model
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.79,0:11:10.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,basically which is super useful for cultural heritage preservation so on top of this we also created the most accurate
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.73,0:11:21.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,model of the Freiburg Cathedral that was depicted on this page over here why this actually was a major stepping
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.07,0:11:30.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,stone towards building self-driving cars and created super useful tools for these vehicles and when it comes to perception,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.67,0:11:36.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,tracking, localization, prediction, planning and control, it also introduced the problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.21,0:11:48.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,The fact that we were relying on these high definition maps actually made these vehicles being bound towards, we call this level 4 automation,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.73,0:11:55.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is basically automation in geofenced areas, which is exactly what you're seeing right now with self-driving cars.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.41,0:12:01.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,You see them in several cities, but you don't see them overall in the world, which would be level 5.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.21,0:12:07.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where do you think are we with robotics right now when it comes to manipulation?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.45,0:12:08.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is who's for level 3?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.92,0:12:12.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe a few level 4?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.16,0:12:14.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Level 5?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.04,0:12:16.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,One.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.18,0:12:25.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are in fact a few applications for this, but I think the major problem there is implementing this everywhere in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.35,0:12:35.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this has been the major challenge, it's also like a driving force for me nowadays, this question of can we actually get rid of these maps.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.59,0:12:45.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,These maps have been super useful and we roboticists like 3D maps simply because it is geometry and we know very well how to deal with geometry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.91,0:12:52.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,roboticists love geometry and by building these maps we turn navigation problems in geometry problems
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.87,0:12:59.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,and there we go there we are with all the constraints regarding the complexity of environments.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.34,0:13:05.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next step in that direction then was like here again is Probabilistic Robotics was
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.66,0:13:09.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,the deep network hype right so when you look back at at the give me
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.02,0:13:15.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,a second Probabilistic Robotics then you basically see that we are particularly bad at this
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.12,0:13:22.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,first step making semantics out of the sensor data like understanding images and understanding point clouds.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.04,0:13:31.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is something that deep networks actually substantially improved and it was a second revolution in this space.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.66,0:13:38.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here's one example for this deep learning application which is semantic segmentation and there
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.58,0:13:44.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,you can basically see that like these systems are substantially better in this interpretation part.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.56,0:13:49.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you agreed with me that they are not as good in localization and mapping.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.02,0:13:55.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then obviously that raises a question like is there a way to combine the two, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.20,0:13:56.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,How can we do this properly?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.72,0:14:06.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is something, a discussion that I also started with colleagues here and we were at a TRI or we worked at TRI building these self-driving cars,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.28,0:14:11.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,namely this question of once we have these super effective segmentation and
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.56,0:14:16.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Perception tools like how can we combine them properly with this probabilistic approach?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.16,0:14:23.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you need there in this context is basically that what is called Calibrated uncertainties and otherwise your filters
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.94,0:14:29.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,or your state estimation processes will basically diverge This problem doesn't go away when you go to foundation models
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.74,0:14:37.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,It becomes even harder because these models are even more complex and like estimating or proper Uncertainties based on
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.94,0:14:43.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,these foundation models is a severe change And here's one example of that what we did in this context,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.96,0:14:50.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,this uncertainty where panoptic segmentation where you basically not only provide
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.03,0:14:56.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,the segmentation masks but you also get these semantic uncertainties for segmentation.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.71,0:15:00.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can also do this for instant segmentation which then turns out to be
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.33,0:15:05.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you combine the two to be just panoptic segmentation or some panoptic uncertainties.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.61,0:15:12.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here you see this in action for like famous data set you can actually see that these
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.51,0:15:21.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,uncertainties arise at places where they actually make sense that's namely at the borders of classes or also objects
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.04,0:15:31.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,right the and the next step was basically the integration of that with one of these state estimation processes
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.34,0:15:37.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,you see in this context a particle filter in which case you would actually you actually need to estimate
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.08,0:15:44.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,a regularizer that takes the uncertainties that are generated by the networks in order to convert them into
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.70,0:15:49.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,calibrated uncertainties which is something that you actually need to learn and when you do this in a proper
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.44,0:15:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,fashion then you can actually have probabilistic localization at a higher accuracy based on these deep network outputs or
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.16,0:16:08.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,learned outputs from directly from the data into segmentation mask and other features that you are actually interested in.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.72,0:16:20.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which brings me to this this other problem in this context right so what we did in this deep learning phase was basically we were in the
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.29,0:16:26.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,belief that we can actually solve all these problems using deep learning with
